# Hash-manifested fixture files must reach the working tree byte-identical to their
# committed blobs on every platform (TEST-D47's sha256 custody would otherwise break
# under core.autocrlf=true checkouts, observed live: all five M3-B07 corpus .ron
# files failed manifest verification on Windows purely through LF->CRLF rewriting).
crates/testing/gametest/corpus/** text eol=lf
crates/testing/rc-golden-data/fixtures/** -text
# M3.5-B01: same class of bug, same fix -- `crates/registries/generated/**` is the
# other TEST-D47 hash-manifested tree (MANIFEST.json + its generated Rust), and was
# missing this rule (confirmed live on this machine: registries.rs/block_states.rs/
# tags.rs, all pre-dating this blueprint, already failed manifest verification here
# purely through LF->CRLF checkout rewriting, before this blueprint's own new fourth
# file was ever generated).
crates/registries/generated/** text eol=lf
